  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array AAA of length NNN such that 1≤Ai≤N1 \\leq A_i \\leq N1≤Ai​≤N and Ai≠i,A_i \\neq i,Ai​=i, ∀i∈[1,N]\\forall i \\in [1, N]∀i∈[1,N].\n\nCount the number of arrays BBB of length NNN such that ∀i∈[1,N]\\forall i \\in [1, N]∀i∈[1,N]:\n\n\nBi≠BAiB_i \\neq B_{A_i}Bi​=BAi​​\n1≤Bi≤M1 \\leq B_i \\leq M1≤Bi​≤M\nSince the answer may be large, print it modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT − the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nEach test case contains 222 lines of input:\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space separated integers NNN, MMM.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer on a newline - answer modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "1≤M≤1001 \\leq M \\leq 1001≤M≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤N,Ai≠i1 \\leq A_i \\leq N, A_i \\neq i1≤Ai​≤N,Ai​=i",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
